// ============================================================================
//  PAC-MAN '80 — Perchance Edition
//  A complete recreation of the 1980 arcade classic Pac-Man, built on
//  perchance.org with the Perchance AI Helper.
//
//  This file currently holds the ROADMAP for the build (see the `roadmap`
//  list at the bottom). Backlog generated with the atomic-roadmap
//  methodology (perchance.org/atomic-roadmap): dependency-ordered phases of
//  atomic, agent-ready tasks. Check a task off ([x]) as the AI helper
//  completes it. Phases 1-7 build the full game.
// ============================================================================

$meta
  title = PAC-MAN '80 — Perchance Edition
  description = A complete recreation of the 1980 arcade classic Pac-Man, built on perchance.org with the Perchance AI Helper. Maze-chase gameplay, ghosts with the original AI, synthesized arcade audio.
  image = https://user.uploads.dev/file/023691ad1fa50f171208ddd72b0db642.png
  tags = game, arcade, pac-man, retro, 1980, maze, ai helper
  header
    mode = minimal

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ROADMAP — work through these in order (index.html renders this checklist)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
roadmap
  ## PHASE 1 — Branding & App Shell
  1. \[x\] **Brand the generator:** `$meta` title/description/tags/image, arcade palette (black + Pac-Man yellow), retro font, logo in the header. (done)
  2. \[x\] **Scaffold the shell in index.html:** full-screen `<canvas>` game surface, HUD bar (score / high score / lives), hidden overlays (title, ready, game over), responsive CSS.
  3. \[x\] **Game-loop driver:** `requestAnimationFrame` + fixed-timestep update, devicePixelRatio-aware canvas scaling, pause flag, frame-rate-independent movement.
  4. \[x\] **Title / attract screen:** "INSERT COIN — PRESS ENTER" screen that starts the game on Enter or tap, with a high-score readout.

  ## PHASE 2 — Maze & Tile Engine
  5. \[x\] **Maze data:** encode the classic 28×31 maze as a string-tile grid (walls, dots, power pellets, ghost house + door, side tunnels) in main.pjs.
  6. \[x\] **Tile loader:** parse the grid into a 2D walkable array; helpers `tileAt(x,y)`, `isWall`, pixel↔tile conversion; tunnel rows wrap.
  7. \[x\] **Render the maze:** thick rounded blue walls, small dots, blinking power pellets, ghost-house door line, tunnel openings; correct draw order (floor, dots, walls, entities).
  8. \[x\] **Fruit slots:** target cells for fruit spawns, timed despawn logic, fruit draw.

  ## PHASE 3 — Pac-Man Movement
  9. \[x\] **Tile-based movement:** continuous inter-tile movement with center snapping, buffered direction input, no instant 180° reversal, corner-turn assist.
  10. \[x\] **Tunnel wrap:** wrap from the left edge to the right edge and vice versa on the tunnel rows.
  11. \[x\] **Animation:** 2-frame open/close mouth timed to speed, facing direction, mouth held open during frightened mode.
  12. \[x\] **Eating:** pellet/dot consumption on tile enter, dot counting (for fruit triggers), score per pellet, waka-waka cadence hook.
  13. \[x\] **Death sequence:** freeze, chomp-animation pause, lives decrement, "READY!" respawn, or GAME OVER when lives run out.

  ## PHASE 4 — Ghosts & AI
  14. \[x\] **Ghost entity system:** Blinky (red), Pinky (pink), Inky (cyan), Clyde (orange); per-ghost body/direction/eyes rendering and home-corner targets.
  15. \[x\] **Intersection AI:** score-based direction choice (prefer target tile, no reversal), facing-corner special case, tunnel + ghost-house-door handling.
  16. \[x\] **Targeting logic:** Blinky → direct chase; Pinky → 4 tiles ahead of Pac-Man; Inky → 2-ahead vector mirrored by Blinky; Clyde → chase when far (>8 tiles), retreat to corner when near (classic).
  17. \[x\] **Scatter/chase schedule:** timed phase switches (7/20/7/20/5/infinite) with per-level durations and a global slowdown on every level after the 1st.
  18. \[x\] **Frightened mode:** power pellet flips ghosts to blue/flashing, random direction at intersections, speed cut, eat for 200/400/800/1600 pts, then eyes return to the ghost house.
  19. \[x\] **Ghost house:** start order + exit timers, eyes-to-house re-entry and respawn, one-way door, level-based release cadence.
  20. \[x\] **Elroy mode:** Blinky speeds up when remaining dots hit the 20/10 thresholds.

  ## PHASE 5 — Game Loop, Scoring & Levels
  21. \[x\] **Scoring:** dot 10, power pellet 50, ghost 200→1600 (combo), fruit points; score + high score in the HUD; extra life at 10,000.
  22. \[x\] **Fruit spawns:** cherry at 70 dots, strawberry at 170, level-appropriate fruits, despawn timer, 100–5000 point values.
  23. \[x\] **Level progression:** on clear, "LEVEL N" intermission (with fruit bonus preview), next maze loads; speeds/durations/fruit escalate per level (caps at level 17+).
  24. \[x\] **Game-over flow:** death animation → "GAME OVER" → title; high score persisted via localStorage; "start at level" dev shortcut (?level via URL, or pm80StartLevel).
  25. \[x\] **Ready/Go state machine:** "READY!" pause before control unlock + "GO!" flash, pause (P/Esc), sound-toggle (M) and fullscreen (F) buttons in the HUD.

  ## PHASE 6 — Audio (WebAudio synth, no assets)
  26. \[x\] **SFX synth:** waka-waka (alternating-pitch chomp), power-pellet drone, eat-ghost sting, fruit chime, extra-life jingle, death arpeggio, level-start jingle.
  27. \[x\] **Audio manager:** init on first user gesture, master on/off toggle persisted, mute when the tab is hidden, gain control.

  ## PHASE 7 — Polish & Release
  28. \[x\] **Retro presentation:** subtle CRT scanlines, arcade-frame vignette, 4:3 feel; keep optional and off by default for accessibility.
  29. \[x\] **Controls & mobile:** arrow keys / WASD, on-screen D-pad + swipe for touch, prevent arrow-key page scroll, responsive scaling on all screens.
  30. \[x\] **QA & spec pass:** verify timing constants vs 1980 specs (speeds, ghost timers, fruit values), ghost-reversal edge cases, cornering feel; squash console errors.
  31. \[x\] **Ship:** `$meta.image` listing screenshot, final title-screen polish, publish.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2 — MAZE DATA (task 5)
// The classic 28×31 tile grid, reconstructed from the Pac-Man Dossier's
// legal-space map (28 cols × 31 rows; one tunnel row passing the ghost house).
// Legend:
//   #  wall                     .  dot (10 pts)          o  power pellet (50 pts)
//   ~  walkable, no pellet (tunnels, corridors, ghost-house interior)
//   D  ghost-house door (ghosts pass; Pac-Man cannot)
//   P  Pac-Man start (has a dot)     F  fruit slot (has a dot)
//   G  ghost start (Blinky above the house; Pinky/Inky/Clyde inside)
